  "title": "Generation gets one front door",
  "summary": "Generation found a single API home while models, media tools, and app setup gained more room to work.\n\nImage, video, text, chat, and speech generation moved to gen.pollinations.ai, along with the interactive API reference. Text generation joined Gen’s Worker with streaming support; image and video handlers followed into the gateway. Redirects preserve query strings and POST requests from legacy Enter generation URLs.\n\nDeepSeek Pro’s registered context grew from 65,536 to 1,048,576 tokens. The lineup also gained Llama 3.3 70B Instruct and paid-balance GPT-5.5, while Grok 4.20’s metadata now lists image input and a 262,144-token context. Routing fixes addressed DeepSeek Pro, Grok, and several other models.\n\nNova Reel gained reproducible seeds and durations up to 120 seconds in six-second steps. Grok Imagine gained single-reference-image edits, including uploads in Play. Qwen instruct speech gained an instruction parameter, and AssemblyAI Universal-2 and Universal-3 Pro joined the transcription endpoint with text, JSON, and subtitle output.\n\nBYOP consent now identifies apps by client ID or app key rather than matching URLs, and publishable app keys can register multiple authorized callbacks. Key creation validates permissions and metadata up front. The community-maintained OpenClaw guide gained a Pollinations Connect flow that fills its setup examples with the returned key.",
